cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenRaceStack or ApexPathAI in your academic or industrial research, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenRaceStack: A Modular, Cross-Platform Autonomous Racing Framework for Multi-Scale Vehicles"
version: 1.0.0-rc1
date-released: "2026-11-15"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/apexpath-ai/ApexPathAI"
url: "https://github.com/apexpath-ai/ApexPathAI"
abstract: >-
  OpenRaceStack is an open-source, modular, cross-platform autonomous racing framework
  and proving ground validation platform designed for multi-scale vehicles (1:10 scale F1TENTH,
  electric go-karts, Dallara AV-21 IndyCars, and passenger GT racecars). The framework provides
  high-rate dynamic bicycle models with Pacejka tires, real-time Frenet-frame Model Predictive
  Control (<2 ms solve latency), quintic/quartic Frenet lattice trajectory planning,
  2D LiDAR SVD-ICP and NDT scan matching, multi-agent racing simulation with aerodynamic
  wake drafting, and recursive least squares system identification and online friction adaptation.
keywords:
  - "autonomous racing"
  - "vehicle dynamics"
  - "model predictive control"
  - "frenet trajectory planning"
  - "state estimation"
  - "system identification"
  - "online adaptation"
  - "multi-agent simulation"
  - "F1TENTH"
  - "Indy Autonomous Challenge"
